    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43775" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septingenti</span></b> , ae, a, num. adj.
		septemcentum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>seven hundred</i>: anni, Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 3, 1, 2</span></i> (Ann. v. 493 Vahl.); cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annorum septingentorum memoria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Or. 34, 120</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nummi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 5, 2, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">milia passuum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Quint. 25, 78</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stadia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 11, § 76</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">milites,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					23, 20, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">naves,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Curt. 10, 1, 19</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septingenta Tito debet Lupus (sc. sestertia),</span>”
				<i>seven hundred thousand sesterces</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 10, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
